1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:15,000
残酷な天使のように 少年よ 神話になれ

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:29,000
青い風が今 胸のドアを叩いても

3
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:37,000
私だけをただ見つめて 微笑んでるあなた

4
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:44,000
そっと触れるもの 求めることに夢中で

5
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:51,000
運命さえ まだ知らない 痛いけな瞳

6
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:59,000
だけどいつか気づくでしょう その背中には

7
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,000
遥か未来 目指すための羽があること

8
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,000
残酷な天使の手勢 窓辺から

9
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:19,000
やがて飛び立つ 吹き飛ばしる熱いパトスで

10
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:27,000
思い出を裏切るなら この空を抱いて輝く

11
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,000
何故?

12
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,000
お前は一目 悩んだ moments

13
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,000
前後な天使 της

14
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:37,500
Ashino Lakes 2 and 3.

15
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:39,760
I hope we won't have many more holes to fill.

16
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:43,880
Which reminds me, Chairman Keele came to see me yesterday.

17
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:45,860
He was complaining about the delays.

18
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:47,660
He was pretty steamed.

19
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:49,800
He even hinted at your dismissal.

20
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,060
Adam is going well.

21
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:55,360
And work on the dummy plug for the Ava project is proceeding.

22
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:58,900
What are the old men at Zaylay complaining about now?

23
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:03,220
The fact that the instrumentality project is behind schedule?

24
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:06,800
The projects are all linked together. There are no problems.

25
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:07,760
Including Rey?

26
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,160
Well, I won't impress you.

27
00:02:12,140 --> 00:02:14,600
So how will we deal with you-know-who?

28
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:17,680
Let him do as he wishes. The same with the Marduk Institute.

29
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:21,620
I agree. We can make use of him. For a while.

30
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:28,200
What started here?

31
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:31,140
Sixteen years ago.

32
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:52,380
It's me.

33
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:56,400
Ah, so it is.

34
00:02:56,580 --> 00:02:59,300
This is Shannon Bio Inc., a foreign chemical firm.

35
00:02:59,780 --> 00:03:01,480
It's been like this for nine years.

36
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:03,800
Nine years without a single change.

37
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:10,920
So far, 106 corporations out of the 108 affiliated with the Marduk Institute have turned out to be dummy companies.

38
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:13,540
And this one is the 107th.

39
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:15,620
This is the company's registration record.

40
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:18,720
And you want me to take a look at the board of directors, don't you?

41
00:03:18,820 --> 00:03:20,140
You already know about this?

42
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:21,540
I know most of the names.

43
00:03:21,980 --> 00:03:22,280
Yes.

44
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:30,720
The Marduk Institute is supposed to be an advisory body established under the control of the Human Instrumentality Committee for the purpose of selecting Ava pilots.

45
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,660
Something's not adding up right here.

46
00:03:32,660 --> 00:03:34,980
Your task is to investigate the nerve.

47
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:38,320
Getting involved with the Marduk may be an ill-advised step.

48
00:03:38,460 --> 00:03:39,660
Well, I can't help it.

49
00:03:40,340 --> 00:03:44,000
My nose for trouble has a penchant for getting my eyes in the wrong places.

50
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,120
Hi, this is Kaji.

51
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:51,320
I'm out right now, but you can leave your name and a message at the beep.

52
00:03:54,020 --> 00:03:55,480
Help me, Kaji!

53
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:57,380
Don't touch me, you pervert!

54
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:00,120
That ought to do it.

55
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:01,660
What's going on?

56
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:04,100
I was just calling Kaji.

57
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:06,300
I wanted him to take me out tomorrow.

58
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:10,300
I've been calling him and calling him, but he's always out these days.

59
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:13,200
He's always out doing something.

60
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,880
You mean you'll be available tomorrow?

61
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:18,760
Unfortunately, it seems so.

62
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:19,880
Great!

63
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:21,840
Then I've got a favor to ask you.

64
00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:22,140
Huh?

65
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,000
Well, you see...

66
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,400
What?

67
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:27,440
A date?

68
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:33,340
The guy's a friend of Kadama, my big sister, and he keeps asking and asking me to set you and him up.

69
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,420
Pretty please!

70
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:41,240
Huh?

71
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:49,960
Get back to your work!

72
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:50,960
Sorry!

73
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:53,180
Why don't you get back to work, Toji?

74
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:53,680
Don't care!

75
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:55,420
Microsis operation completed.

76
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,100
Inversible graph measurement finalized.

77
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:58,680
Oh, which dress are you wearing?

78
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:00,700
Oh, for the wedding tomorrow?

79
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:07,400
Well, I wore the pink suit for Kiyomi's wedding, and I wore the dark blue dress for Kotoko's shower, and...

80
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:08,540
There's that orange one.

81
00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:09,960
You haven't worn that one lately.

82
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:11,240
The orange one?

83
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:13,400
Well, there's a reason I haven't worn it.

84
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:14,740
It's too tight.

85
00:05:14,740 --> 00:05:15,700
Ah, thank you!

86
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:18,900
Maybe I should just buy a new one.

87
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:22,560
Man, all these stupid weddings are killing my bank account.

88
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:24,200
Tell me about it.

89
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:26,520
We've been to so many showers, I'm almost broke.

90
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:30,460
Yeah, it's like everyone's in a rush to get married before they turn 30.

91
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:33,700
And you don't want to be the last one still single, do you?

92
00:05:33,780 --> 00:05:34,660
Excuse me?

93
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:36,440
Okay, you guys can take off now.

94
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:37,500
Good work.

95
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:39,240
It's about time!

96
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:42,180
These stupid experiments are really getting on my nerves!

97
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:48,700
Speaking of which, Shinji seems more subdued than usual.

98
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:50,720
Tomorrow's the day.

99
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:52,420
Oh, yeah.

100
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:53,520
Tomorrow.

101
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:54,940
Tomorrow.

102
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:58,000
I have to see my father tomorrow.

103
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:01,500
What should I talk to him about, Ray?

104
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:03,240
I don't understand.

105
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:04,600
Why are you asking me?

106
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:08,600
Because I've seen you talking with my father and actually enjoying it.

107
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:15,140
Say, my father, what's he like?

108
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:18,380
I don't know.

109
00:06:20,980 --> 00:06:21,580
Oh.

110
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:25,200
Have you been watching me because you wanted to ask that question?

111
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:26,920
Mm-hmm.

112
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:35,040
Hey, when we were cleaning, that cloth, the way you ringed it, it reminded me of a mother when you squeezed it.

113
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:36,200
A mother?

114
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:37,700
Uh, yeah.

115
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:43,840
It just reminded me of a mom.

116
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:47,520
I bet you'll make a great mother, Ray.

117
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:52,760
I mean, you embarrass me.

118
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:58,440
I'm home.

119
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:00,000
What's happening?

120
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:02,260
You better go to bed, Oscar.

121
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:03,620
Don't you have a date tomorrow?

122
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:05,140
With some med student.

123
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:07,260
Oh, Misato!

124
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:09,740
Can I use your lavender perfume?

125
00:07:10,380 --> 00:07:11,020
Uh, no.

126
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:12,420
No, Nini.

127
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:14,820
That stuff's not for kids.

128
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:16,240
Is Shinji in his room?

129
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:18,540
Yeah, ever since he got home.

130
00:07:18,780 --> 00:07:20,380
I don't think he wants to meet his father.

131
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:23,140
If he hates him so much, why doesn't he just say?

132
00:07:23,420 --> 00:07:25,080
You Japanese are weird.

133
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:27,500
Well, he doesn't actually hate him.

134
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:28,540
That's the problem.

135
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:35,340
Leave.

136
00:07:35,340 --> 00:07:35,400
Leave.

137
00:07:39,420 --> 00:07:41,040
Good work, Shinji.

138
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:44,360
Shinji!

139
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:47,620
I'm coming in, okay?

140
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:55,660
You're worried about seeing your father tomorrow, right?

141
00:07:56,940 --> 00:07:58,760
You mustn't run away, Shinji.

142
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:02,220
Nothing will ever change unless you have the courage to step forward.

143
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:04,720
I know that, Misato.

144
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,720
You're going to find out the truth.

145
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,480
You've got to keep moving forward.

146
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:12,240
After each step, you've got to keep taking another afterwards.

147
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:16,460
Anyway, when you see him tomorrow, you've got to keep your chin held high.

148
00:08:16,880 --> 00:08:18,460
Because you'll be seeing her, too.

149
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:20,320
Good night, Shinji.

150
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:26,680
You bought a new dress, didn't you?

151
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:27,280
Let me see.

152
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:28,660
Oh, you want to see it, do you?

153
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:29,920
It's an expensive one.

154
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:31,500
Price doesn't always be flexible.

155
00:08:31,860 --> 00:08:33,460
Tell me about it.

156
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:34,920
Well, what do you think?

157
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:37,740
Did you pick that one with Paji in mind?

158
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:38,440
Grow up.

159
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:39,480
It was a long time ago.

160
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:42,660
Well, see ya.

161
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:43,260
Later.

162
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:43,820
Aw.

163
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:52,400
You must keep three bags in your heart.

164
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:57,540
And now, let us proceed to the reception.

165
00:08:57,540 --> 00:09:01,380
Little boy Blue is late.

166
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:05,280
That oversexed idiot's never been on time in his whole lazy life.

167
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:06,780
For your dates, you mean?

168
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:08,240
He gets to work early.

169
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:09,700
Hello, girls.

170
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:11,820
You're looking particularly lovely today.

171
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:14,540
I had a little trouble getting out of work on time.

172
00:09:14,640 --> 00:09:17,040
I find that hard to believe since you don't do anything.

173
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:21,080
You could at least have taken the time and trouble to shave that awful stubble.

174
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:22,960
Your tie is crooked.

175
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:25,640
Well, thank you.

176
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:27,400
You act like you're married.

177
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:29,180
You're very astute, Ritsipoo.

178
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:30,920
Who'd marry this bomb?

179
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:48,660
It's been three years since we were last here.

180
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:51,220
That's when I ran away.

181
00:09:51,220 --> 00:09:54,220
I haven't come back here since then.

182
00:09:55,060 --> 00:09:58,340
I just don't believe that my mom is really resting here.

183
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:00,760
I don't even remember her face.

184
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:03,660
Burying memories is man's way of surviving.

185
00:10:04,220 --> 00:10:06,580
But there are some things a man should never forget.

186
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:10,200
Yui taught me that one irreplaceable thing, Shinji.

187
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:13,460
That is the reason I come here, to confirm that commitment.

188
00:10:15,420 --> 00:10:17,120
You don't have a picture of her?

189
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:18,300
No photographs.

190
00:10:18,960 --> 00:10:20,380
Even this grave is an artifice.

191
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:21,600
Nothing remains.

192
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:23,520
That's like my teacher said.

193
00:10:23,740 --> 00:10:25,120
You cast everything away.

194
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:27,380
Everything is kept in my heart.

195
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:29,120
I'm satisfied with that.

196
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:33,280
Our time is up.

197
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:34,600
I'm leaving now.

198
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:42,660
Father!

199
00:10:42,660 --> 00:10:49,600
I'm glad that we could talk together today.

200
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:51,040
Indeed.

201
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:51,760
I'm leaving now.

202
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:52,100
I'm sorry.

203
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:55,000
What?

204
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:37,820
That was very nice, Shinji.

205
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:39,400
I didn't know you played.

206
00:11:39,940 --> 00:11:43,220
I started when I was five, but I'm still not very good.

207
00:11:43,460 --> 00:11:44,960
I have no talent at all.

208
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:46,920
Well, perseverance wins the battle.

209
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:48,220
I'm impressed.

210
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:50,720
I only started because my teachers told me to,

211
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:53,020
but I could have quit any time.

212
00:11:53,140 --> 00:11:54,180
So why didn't you?

213
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:56,780
Huh? Nobody told me to stop, I guess.

214
00:11:56,900 --> 00:11:58,540
Oh, I should have known.

215
00:11:58,940 --> 00:12:00,120
Hey, you're back early.

216
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:02,580
I thought you were going out to dinner, too.

217
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:05,120
Oh, my date was even more boring than you.

218
00:12:05,660 --> 00:12:07,880
So while he was standing in line for the roller coaster,

219
00:12:08,040 --> 00:12:09,320
I took a train back here.

220
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:11,140
That seems kind of cold.

221
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:15,100
Oh, gosh, he's the only real man in my life.

222
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:18,140
I know it's getting a little late,

223
00:12:18,260 --> 00:12:20,020
but I've got to go powder my nose.

224
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:22,520
Making a quick exit?

225
00:12:27,180 --> 00:12:28,320
High heels.

226
00:12:29,780 --> 00:12:32,600
It's been a while since we went out together.

227
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:34,440
She's drinking too much.

228
00:12:34,760 --> 00:12:36,240
She's losing her control.

229
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:39,960
Sometimes you just have to drink to keep yourself under control.

230
00:12:40,780 --> 00:12:41,980
All of us do.

231
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:44,780
Well, you did used to live with her,

232
00:12:44,860 --> 00:12:46,420
so I guess you'd know the truth.

233
00:12:46,420 --> 00:12:48,920
Well, that was a lifetime ago.

234
00:12:49,260 --> 00:12:51,220
She didn't even own a set of heels back then.

235
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:54,600
That's not how we saw it back when we were in school.

236
00:12:54,800 --> 00:12:55,740
We were kids, Ritsu.

237
00:12:56,380 --> 00:12:57,240
That wasn't real.

238
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:59,580
We were just children playing house.

239
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:00,680
It was nice.

240
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:02,580
But life's not that simple.

241
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:04,080
Oh, I almost forgot.

242
00:13:04,420 --> 00:13:05,580
The cat dragged this in.

243
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:08,400
Thank you, Kaji, for being honest.

244
00:13:08,460 --> 00:13:09,320
To the ladies, yes.

245
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:10,880
Otherwise, eh...

246
00:13:10,880 --> 00:13:11,760
I doubt that.

247
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:13,600
And Misato?

248
00:13:13,900 --> 00:13:15,400
I've lost that war before.

249
00:13:15,820 --> 00:13:17,480
Doom battles aren't my style.

250
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:19,220
I think you still have a chance.

251
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:20,240
Well, what about you?

252
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:22,700
Oh, I don't like to talk about myself.

253
00:13:23,100 --> 00:13:24,680
There's nothing much to say.

254
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:26,960
Why is she taking so long?

255
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:28,560
How much makeup can she wear?

256
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:30,040
Hmm.

257
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,840
What were you doing in Kyoto?

258
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:33,940
I wasn't in Kyoto.

259
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:35,880
Don't try to fool me.

260
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:38,760
You'll get your fingers burned if you get too involved in this.

261
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:40,540
That's the advice of a friend.

262
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:44,540
I'd rather be burned by the heat of my passion for you.

263
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:47,540
Well, should I buy you some fireworks, then?

264
00:13:47,940 --> 00:13:48,380
Hello.

265
00:13:48,980 --> 00:13:50,700
Oh, you never change, do you?

266
00:13:51,100 --> 00:13:52,200
Of course I change.

267
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:55,040
The act of living is an embracement of change.

268
